    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["D30", "R60"],
      "pins": ["D30.4", "D30.2", "R60.1", "R60.2"],
      "nets": ["ESTOP_OUT", "Net-(D30-K2)", "/LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV"],
      "observed": "D30 is a dual LED whose second anode (D30 pin 4, A2) is connected directly to ESTOP_OUT. The second cathode (D30 pin 2, K2) connects only through R60 back to the same ESTOP_OUT net. Thus the second LED has both terminals tied to the same net (through a resistor) and no return path to a different rail or signal.",
      "expected": "For the second LED to function as an ESTOP indicator, D30 pin 4 (A2) should be connected to the LED power/control net /LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV (as D30 pin 3/A1 is), with R60 returning the cathode to ESTOP_OUT; alternatively R60 should return to a different rail such as GND if ESTOP_OUT is intended to be the anode. The netlist pin functions explicitly label D30 pin 4 as A2, not a cathode.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(libpart (lib \"cm4-robot\") (part \"LED_Dual_KKAA\") ... (pins (pin (num \"3\") (name \"A1\") ...) (pin (num \"4\") (name \"A2\") ...)))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"67\") (name \"ESTOP_OUT\") ... (node (ref \"D30\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"A2\") ...) ... (node (ref \"R60\") (pin \"2\") ...))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"129\") (name \"Net-(D30-K2)\") (node (ref \"D30\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"K2\") ...) (node (ref \"R60\") (pin \"1\") ...))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"31\") (name \"/LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV\") ... (node (ref \"D30\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"A1\") ...))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The second LED in D30 cannot light because it is effectively connected across the same node. If D30 was intended to provide an e-stop/status indication from ESTOP_OUT, that visual indication will be missing, making the board behave differently from the intended design.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows a clear connectivity anomaly on D30: its second anode and second cathode are both tied back to ESTOP_OUT through R60, leaving that LED with no voltage across it. This prevents the intended ESTOP status LED from operating."
}

